# Mixed-license scope notice

This notice separates three kinds of repository material. Kyle Turchick licenses the listed project-authored software under the MIT License. He licenses the listed documentation, figures, tables, annotations, and newly derived results under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), but only to the extent that he owns or controls the applicable rights. The 407 redistributed inputs are outside both project grants; the repository relies on the CC BY 4.0 treatment declared by the cited Pellett–Valbuena Zenodo records. The complete unmodified Open Source Initiative MIT text, with the copyright notice completed, follows this scope notice.

## 1. MIT-licensed Software

For this repository, “Software” in the MIT text below means only the project-authored portions of these materials:

- the following 13 `.R` files under `code/`, including project-authored comments and literal strings:
  - `code/R/00_setup_paths.R`;
  - `code/R/01_packages.R`;
  - `code/R/02_io_lock_metadata.R`;
  - `code/R/03_source_data_prep.R`;
  - `code/R/04_pellett_valbuena_replication.R`;
  - `code/R/05_delta_hdr_model_helpers.R`;
  - `code/R/06_brief_analysis_hierarchy.R`;
  - `code/R/07_brief_deliverables.R`;
  - `code/R/08_validation_helpers.R`;
  - `code/export_figure_table_source_data.R`;
  - `code/run_delta_hdr_brief_reanalysis.R`;
  - `code/run_pellett_valbuena_replication.R`; and
  - `code/run_reanalysis.R`;
- `.gitignore`;
- `.mi_hdr_project_root`;
- the three tracked directory markers:
  - `data/external/pellett_valbuena_2025/01_concept/.gitkeep`;
